        "original_id": "0a14ce13-c9ff-56b0-bd89-fb17215ab3c3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Abraham Bankier, Oskar Schindler\n- Places: Cracow, Poland; Lipowa Street; occupied Poland; Protectorate of Bohemia and Moravia\n- Companies: Rekord factory\n- Roles: industrialist, spy, Nazi Party member, factory owner\n- Events: World War II, the Holocaust\n\nFacts:\n- Abraham Bankier lived from 1910 to 1956.\n- Oskar Schindler lived from 28 April 1908 to 9 October 1974.\n- Before Oskar Schindler took it over during World War II, Abraham Bankier was one of the owners of the Rekord factory on Lipowa Street in Cracow, Poland.\n- Oskar Schindler was a German industrialist, spy, and member of the Nazi Party.\n- During the Holocaust, Oskar Schindler is credited with saving 1,200 Jews by employing them in his enamelware and ammunitions factories in occupied Poland and the Protectorate of Bohemia and Moravia.",
